{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"Receipt confirms the margin generalization. Writing the interpretation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR=\\\"f82d709e8f5f4f80ba19cc48ff29ff0a\\\"\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpretation of the margin receipt \\\"+R+\\\" (completed, exit_code 0) for the wedge investigation. Parsed events: peer_loss_after_wedge at indices 3 and 7 are the three-voter control and faulted steps, 15 and 16 the five-voter control steps, and 20 and 21 the five-voter faulted steps; the truncation phases precede each and re-witness the wedge. The measurement confirms the margin generalisation recorded with the investigation: the wedged replica costs exactly one unit of failure margin in both sizes. The knowledge entry for the margin behaviour is updated to the same statement with the executed observations attached.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"0bfc2ea5a9e94316982943d306eefbf6-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"adeee037edde49b8b2eb64b8278a2187-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"commitment-recalculate-quorum\\\",\\\"commitment-set-configuration\\\",\\\"appendentries-conflict-truncate-block\\\",\\\"appendentries-store-failure-todo\\\",\\\"appendentries-entry-loop-cached-lastlog\\\",\\\"replication-nextindex-floor\\\",\\\"inmem-store-getlog-missing\\\",\\\"state-getlastentry\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{R:[15,16,20,21,3,7]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"3c9253570cfc4de4aef0549f41a050d1-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"A wedged replica holds one commitment slot at its stuck index and therefore consumes exactly one unit of the configuration's failure margin.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"bbd3f51dd21745fb821f9adb6ea7d352-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"One allowed StoreLogs error after a conflicting-suffix deletion leaves the follower unable to converge, and removing the error does not restore progress.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"b7e0a0828e794c5fa40df351cb813d8f-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The reject branch floors nextIndex and re-sends the same request; a snapshot is only produced from the leader's own log store.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Five-voter control (indices 15 and 16): removing one voter still commits the applied entry (commit index 5 to 6, apply future completed with no error) and removing a second voter commits the next one as well (6 to 7, future completed), with the leader's store reaching 1..7 and the follower that takes the wedged role in the control following to the same values; the control therefore tolerates two voter losses. Five-voter faulted (indices 20 and 21): after one voter is removed the entry still commits (5 to 6, future completed) even though the wedged replica is present, but after a second removal the leader's log advances to index 7 (store 1..7, certificate (7,3)) while its commit index stays 6 in every sample of the 1500 ms window and the apply future never completes. The wedged replica's own probe is identical at both steps (store first 1, last 2, certificate (4,2), GetLog of the certificate index reporting 'log not found', StoreLogs attempts 3 and delivered 2, commit and applied 2), so its slot is frozen at the index it held before the wedge. Three-voter baseline (indices 3 and 7): the control commits after its single removal (5 to 6) while the faulted cluster stalls at the same step (commit stays 5, future never completes). Reading the two sizes together: the faulted configuration always stalls exactly one removal earlier than the healthy configuration of the same size, which is the measured form of the margin generalisation. Mechanism, source-backed: commitment takes one match index per voter of the current configuration and requires a quorum of them to reach the entry, so a voter whose durable log cannot advance keeps occupying its slot at the frozen index; the remaining voters must therefore be able to form a quorum without it. Predicate evaluated: a wedged replica must not reduce the configuration's failure margin. It is contradicted in both measured sizes, and the reduction is exactly one unit. Scope: three- and five-voter configurations, in-memory transport, deterministic single StoreLogs error, one process, escalation performed by removing voters at the transport level rather than by stopping their processes.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The reduction is exactly the one slot the wedged replica occupies, so the finding is a margin statement rather than a claim that the wedge collapses a cluster: a five-voter cluster with a wedged replica still commits while three healthy voters answer, and even a three-voter cluster keeps committing while both other voters answer.\\\",\n   \\\"The control in the same execution commits in the same steps up to one removal later, so the stalled commits are not an artefact of removing transports or of the in-process harness.\\\",\n   \\\"The removed voters keep their membership and continue campaigning as lone candidates (visible in the earlier receipt), which did not depose the leader during the windows, so they are not a competing cause; the stall is explained by the match-index arithmetic.\\\",\n   \\\"The wedge itself still requires the exact combination staged here (a conflicting-suffix truncation followed by an allowed StoreLogs error), and a restart repairs it, so the margin loss persists only for an operator who neither restarts the replica nor replaces it.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"Two configuration sizes were measured (three and five voters) with one or two removals respectively; the general statement 'exactly one unit' is inferred from those two sizes and the commitment arithmetic, not from every size.\\\",\n   \\\"The escalation removes voters by disconnecting their transports rather than stopping their processes, so the removed nodes keep running and campaigning; that does not affect the quorum arithmetic but is a difference from a real failure.\\\",\n   \\\"Each step was observed for 1500 ms with 25 ms sampling; a slower commit or a later snapshot-driven repair beyond the window is not claimed.\\\",\n   \\\"One retained execution per case, in-memory transport, deterministic fault injection on a single node, default protocol version.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"被卡死副本确切地消耗一份故障余量：五节点集群仅能再容错一台，对照组可容错两台\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"针对第二条发现的余量推广，本次保留执行 \\\"+R+\\\" 在同一套合法历史（分区、分歧、更高任期替换）上把规模参数化后得到确证：五节点对照组中，移除 1 台投票者后新条目仍提交（commit 5→6），再移除 1 台（共 2 台）后仍提交（6→7）；五节点故障组中，移除 1 台时仍能提交（5→6），再移除 1 台（共 2 台）时领导者自身日志已到 index 7（store 1..7、证书 (7,3)），但 1500 毫秒窗口内 commit 恒为 6、客户端 future 永不完成。三节点基线同样如此：对照组移除 1 台可提交，故障组移除 1 台即停摆。被卡死副本的探针在各步骤中完全不变（store last 2、证书 (4,2)、GetLog 报 log not found、StoreLogs 尝试次数停 3）。结论：卡死副本的承诺槽位被冻结在旧下标，因此确切消耗一份故障余量——三节点集群失去单点容错，五节点集群从『可容错两台』降为『仅能容错一台』；该余量损失持续到该副本被重启（同盘重启已证实可修复）或被替换为止。缺陷主张维持，余量结论以两种规模与提交法定人数算术为依据。\\\"\n }],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\n  \\\"id\\\":\\\"3c9253570cfc4de4aef0549f41a050d1-knowledge-0\\\",\n  \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"commitment keeps one match index per voter of the current configuration and takes the quorum match index as the middle of the sorted values, so a voter whose stored log can never advance holds its slot at the stuck index for as long as the configuration stands. The wedged replica therefore consumes exactly one unit of the configuration's failure margin: the remaining voters must be able to form a quorum on their own, which in a three-voter configuration is impossible once one other voter is gone and in a five-voter configuration only becomes impossible when two other voters are gone.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Leader state; a voter whose durable log is stuck below the leader's committed prefix while it remains a member of configurations.latest; commitment.setConfiguration has been applied for that configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"commitment-recalculate-quorum\\\",\\\"commitment-set-configuration\\\",\\\"appendentries-entry-loop-cached-lastlog\\\",\\\"replication-nextindex-floor\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{R:[15,16,20,21,3,7]}\n }]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('ok', json.load(open('update.json'))['interpretations'][0]['conclusion'], list(json.load(open('update.json'))['interpretations'][0]['executions'].keys()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
